<section class="px-4 md:px-16 mb-16 md:mb-[120px]">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-4 md:gap-8 items-start">
        <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-4">
            <div class="hard-shadow-sm">
                <img
                    alt="Glenn Dyer, author"
                    class="w-full h-auto transition-all duration-700"
                    src="/glenn_dyer_brick_wall.jpg"
                />
            </div>
        </div>

        <div
            class="col-span-12 md:col-span-7 md:col-start-6 flex flex-col justify-center pt-4"
        >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
                <div class="w-10 h-0.5 bg-secondary"></div>
                <span
                    class="font-label-caps text-base text-secondary tracking-widest"
                    >AUTHOR</span
                >
            </div>
            <h1
                class="font-headline-xl text-headline-xl text-primary font-bold tracking-tight mb-6"
            >
                Glenn Dyer
            </h1>
            <p
                class="font-label-caps text-label-caps text-on-surface-variant tracking-widest mb-8"
            >
                THE CONOR THORN SERIES
            </p>
            <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-5">
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    Writing The Torch Betrayal, the first in a series of novels
                    that feature OSS Agent Conor Thorn, allowed Glenn Dyer to
                    immerse himself in the cataclysmic, world-shaping event
                    that was World War II — a subject that has fascinated me
                    since my youth.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    The period of the 1930's and the war years of 1939 to
                    1945, to this day, still produce multitudes of histories,
                    stories, biographies, and memoirs. The availability of
                    once secret documents from the archives of Great Britain,
                    the United States and other countries involved in the
                    conflict, have proved to be a trove of fascinating facts
                    and information.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    Over the years, Dyer's research of World War II has taken
                    him to hotbeds of wartime activity such as Paris, Lyon,
                    Lisbon, London, Normandy, and Rome. Dyer admits that the
                    research phase of writing the novels in the Conor Thorn
                    Series is the most enjoyable phase. Actually, too
                    enjoyable as it keeps him from diving into the outlining
                    (yes, he outlines!) and writing phases. When he is
                    researching, Dyer is looking for little known mysteries
                    that sprouted event that occurred in the European
                    Theatre. Mysteries that seemed to have no final outcomes,
                    thereby inspiring a writer like Dyer to offer up
                    fictional conclusions that he hopes are compelling and
                    entertaining.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    Dyer's professional career has been spent in the
                    commercial broadcasting business, primarily with Fox
                    Television Stations, Inc. serving as the vice president
                    and general manager of four of their TV stations, most
                    recently WTTG Fox 5 and WDCA My20 in Washington D.C.
                    Serving as a general manager for eighteen years, he
                    oversaw all aspects of running large media organizations.
                    While in Washington, DC, among his numerous
                    responsibilities, he wrote editorials for countless
                    newscasts, but his primary passion has always been
                    writing fiction.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    The four books in the Conor Thorn Series have been well
                    received by readers and editorial organizations such as
                    Kirkus, Foreword/Clarion, Military Writers Society of
                    America, Best Thriller Books, BookLife/Publishers Weekly,
                    Indie Reader, Book Trib, BlueInk Reviews, and The Real
                    Book Spy. He is very grateful that bestselling authors
                    such as Steve Berry, Jack Carr, James R. Benn, and Alex
                    Finlay have been kind enough to lend some praise in
                    regard to the series.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    The most recent novel in the Conor Thorn Series, Trust No
                    One, was an Award Finalist for Historical Fiction from
                    the Military Writers Society of America, was short
                    listed in the 2023 Hemingway Award for 20th Century
                    Wartime Fiction and was a finalist in the 2023 Global
                    Thriller Awards for High Stakes Suspense Fiction.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    After thirty-seven years in the broadcasting industry,
                    his wife Chris and he moved back to Park City, Utah where
                    I have been writing full time. I miss living in such a
                    dynamic city as Washington, DC, but relish our time in
                    the mountain desert.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    They have three children, Thomas, Michael and Riley, and
                    four beautiful grandchildren. All of whom live too far
                    away.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    Dyer is an active member of the International Thriller
                    Writers, The Authors Guild, and The OSS Society. He
                    attended Villanova University and graduated from Boston
                    University with a Bachelor of Science degree in
                    Broadcasting & Film.
                </p>
                <p
                    class="font-body-lg text-body-lg text-on-surface-variant leading-relaxed"
                >
                    He looks back fondly on his years growing up in the
                    great state of New Jersey.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
